M5Stack firmware archive

The sketches come from the pinned M5Stack Arduino documentation revisions
recorded in the case manifests. The earlier CoreS3 and Cardputer-ADV
firmware uses 6ee4f2fb9dca1c671e475407cb709109a699cf1a. Each firmware.json identifies
the English page, source section and any linked library example.
Copyright and applicable terms remain with the respective rightsholders.
The M5Unified WAV sketch uses the documented Cardputer-Adv chip select
and the generated SD audio fixture. The LTR5XX manifest pins the original
documentation download and its checksum.

M5Unified, M5GFX, M5Cardputer and Arduino-IRremote are MIT licensed.
Their notices are under licenses/. The manifests identify M5Unit-Sonic
where used. The shipped Arduino-ESP32 source in M5Stack board package
3.2.5 includes LGPL-2.1-or-later code. The ESP-IDF SDK includes Apache-2.0
code and components with separate licenses.
https://m5stack.oss-cn-shenzhen.aliyuncs.com/resource/arduino/m5stack-3.2.5.zip
https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/tree/858a988d

The public BIN and ELF files are rebuilt outputs of those sketches and
components. See build-records/rebuild-2026-11-26.md for exact source
revisions and commands to rebuild or relink with modified sources.
The manifests preserve the original-build hashes and flash layouts.

UIFlow2 v2.5.3 is an official M5Stack release artifact. Its original bytes
are available from M5Burner via the URL in the manifest.

The CoreS3 replay runner adapts the pinned esp32sim runner. Its MIT notice
is under licenses/. The SD media, camera patterns and input tones were
generated for virtual-device validation.

The expanded matrix records its library revisions and checksums in
build-records/arduino-matrix-library-lock.json. The Cardputer-ADV UIFlow2
entries preserve example source and validation metadata. Stock UIFlow2
images remain at the official download URLs listed in the manifests.
